            <ArticleTitle>Eagle's syndrome. Review of the literature and a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>30-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Eagle's syndrome has received scant attention in both medical and dental literature. The symptoms related to this condition can be confused with those attributed to a wide variety of facial neuralgias. The present case refers to a 46-year-old white woman with the symptomatology of Eagle's syndrome, especially the carotid artery type.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
